  "id": "DrugBank_DB00681 - MONDO_44070",
  "verbalization": "Amphotericin B is implicated in the treatment of candidiasis through multiple indirect pathways, as evidenced by its association with Disseminated Candidiasis, Coccidioidomycosis, and Histoplasmosis. These conditions are all linked to Itraconazole, which in turn is associated with Candidemia. The evidence suggests that Amphotericin B may indirectly contribute to the development of Candidemia through the pathophysiological effects of the infections it treats, which may involve immune modulation or antifungal activity. The shared pathway from these infections to Candidemia implies a potential mechanism where the treatment of fungal infections with Amphotericin B could influence the progression of candidiasis, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence supports a relationship between Amphotericin B and Candidemia through a chain of indications involving Itraconazole, highlighting a possible role in the pathogenesis of candidemia.",
